      "candidates": [
        {
          "entry_id": 2731,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.5936568,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "Question: How much will my visit cost if I am paying out-of-pocket?\nAnswer: Out-of-pocket rates are $120 for a General Practitioner (GP) visit, $180 for a Dentist appointment, and $160 for all other specialist consultations.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2744,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.47880465,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "# Procedure codes and self-pay prices\n\nYour itemized receipt lists each procedure done at your visit by its billing code. Medical procedures use five-digit CPT codes, and dental procedures use CDT codes that start with the letter D. If you pay out of pocket, each procedure below is charged at the price shown, in addition to the rate for the visit at which it is done.\n\n## Medical procedures\n\n- 93000: resting 12-lead electrocardiogram, with the doctor's reading of it - $65\n- 94010: spirometry - $85\n- 93784: 24-hour ambulatory blood pressure monitoring - $140\n- 81002: urine dipstick test done in the clinic - $15\n- 69210: ear wax removal, per ear - $75\n- 17110: wart freezing (cryotherapy), up to 14 warts in one session - $90\n\n## Dental procedures\n\n- D2391: tooth-coloured filling on one surface of a back tooth - $210\n- D2140: silver (amalgam) filling on one surface - $160\n- D7140: simple tooth extraction - $240\n\n## A code you do not recognise\n\n",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2743,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.42086348,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "# General practice services\n\n## Annual physical examination\n\nAn annual physical is a preventive check-up for adults who feel well. It includes a review of your medical history and current medicines; your blood pressure, heart rate, height, weight and body mass index (BMI); a physical examination; and a discussion of the screening tests and vaccinations recommended for your age. Most insurance plans cover one preventive physical a year at no cost to you, but check with your plan.\n\n## Long-term conditions\n\nIf you live with a long-term condition such as type 2 diabetes, high blood pressure, asthma or COPD, your GP will agree a regular review schedule with you, usually every three or six months. Bring your home blood pressure or blood glucose readings to each review, and bring your inhalers if you have asthma or COPD, so the GP can check your technique.\n\n## Ear wax removal\n\n",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2730,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.4201032,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "Question: What should I do if my insurance isn't listed or I am out-of-network?\nAnswer: You can pay out-of-pocket for your visit, and we can provide you with an itemized receipt to submit to your insurer for potential reimbursement.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2744,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.41500893,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": " a back tooth - $210\n- D2140: silver (amalgam) filling on one surface - $160\n- D7140: simple tooth extraction - $240\n\n## A code you do not recognise\n\nIf your receipt shows a code that is not in this list, the front desk can tell you what it is.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2738,
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "similarity_score": 0.40555793,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "vaccine $35, high-dose flu vaccine $70, Tdap $55, hepatitis A $85 per dose, typhoid injection $90, oral typhoid course $95, hepatitis B $70 per dose. They are the price of the vaccine itself, and are ",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2735,
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "similarity_score": 0.40001088,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": " is not in-network. AARP Medicare Advantage plans from UnitedHealthcare are in-network when the plan is a PPO, and not in-network when it is an HMO.\n\n## Medicare and Medicaid\n\nWe accept Original Medic",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2743,
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "similarity_score": 0.38839042,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "hree weeks apart. We do not remove skin tags, moles or other skin lesions for cosmetic reasons.\n\n## Medical examinations for work, driving and sport\n\nWe do not carry out commercial driver (DOT) medica",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2732,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.38749894,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: When is payment due, and what payment methods do you accept?\nAnswer: Payment is due at the time of service. We accept cash, major credit and debit cards (Visa, Mastercard, American Express),",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2741,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.36559105,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": " your last name and date of birth. The kiosk cannot take payments: any copay or self-pay amount is paid at the front desk.\n\n## Language interpreters\n\nFree telephone interpreting is available in more t",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2726,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.35367167,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: Do I need a referral from a primary care doctor to book with a specialist?\nAnswer: You can book a visit with any of our practitioners without a referral.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2743,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.34926268,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "r blood glucose readings to each review, and bring your inhalers if you have asthma or COPD, so the GP can check your technique.\n\n## Ear wax removal\n\nWe remove ear wax by microsuction, which uses a sm",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2741,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.33384502,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Checking in and registering\n\n## Registering as a new patient\n\nNew patients fill in three forms at their first visit:\n\n- Form PR-1, New Patient Registration: your contact details, emergency contact a",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2735,
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "similarity_score": 0.31742984,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": " visit at check-in. The front desk can estimate that amount for you if you give them your plan details before the visit.\n\n## Updating your insurance\n\nIf your insurance has changed since your last visi",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2738,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.31546402,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "ome vaccines need more than one dose or take time to become effective. Bring your travel dates and the list of countries you are visiting. We offer:\n\n- hepatitis A (Havrix): two doses six to twelve mo",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2728,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.31107423,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: Do you offer virtual or telehealth consultations?\nAnswer: No, we currently only offer in-person visits at our clinic location.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2733,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.29441768,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: What are your clinic hours and locations?\nAnswer: We are open Monday through Saturday from 9:00 AM to 6:00 PM at 15a Willson St. The nearest free parking is a 3-minute walk away at the Mega ",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2742,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.28739727,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "ltation for your personal use, as long as you tell the practitioner before you start. Staff and other patients must not be recorded or photographed.\n\n## How long we keep records\n\nWe keep adult medical",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2742,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.2862562,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Your privacy and your health information\n\n## Who can see your medical record\n\nYour record can be seen only by the practitioners and staff involved in your care at the clinic, and by the staff who ha",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2739,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.28091633,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Running late\n\n## If you are running late\n\nCall the front desk on (212) 555-0142 as soon as you know you will be late, so we can tell the practitioner and plan around it. The phone line is answered M",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2727,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.27774513,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: What should I bring to my first appointment?\nAnswer: Please bring a valid photo ID, your insurance card, and any relevant prior lab or test results related to your case.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2734,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.2738443,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: How early should I arrive before my scheduled appointment time?\nAnswer: If it is your first visit to our clinic, please arrive 15 minutes before your appointment time to complete your regist",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2740,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.26695475,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Appointment reminders and messages from the clinic\n\n## Text message reminders\n\nWe send a reminder by text message 48 hours before your appointment and another 2 hours before it. Our messages always ",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2739,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.26036364,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": " room has to be prepared and cleaned between patients.\n\n## If the clinic is running late\n\nSometimes an earlier appointment takes longer than planned. If your practitioner is running more than 20 minut",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2736,
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "similarity_score": 0.2584987,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "d on the other side of your mouth for the first few days. For pain, use the over-the-counter painkiller the dentist recommended at your appointment.\n\nContact us if the bleeding has not stopped after f",
          "text_truncated": true
        }
      ],
